--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Purpose

This thorn tests the loop_outermost_int constructs by filling the outermost "boundary" points in the interior, which can be used for evolved boundary conditions (e.g. radiative boundary conditions, which are implemented in SpacetimeX/NewRadX).

The thorn also pins the partition of a grid function component by the device-only primitives loop_allmn_device(ord) and loop_outer_n_device(ord), and the equality of loop_allm1_device with loop_allmn_device(1), on a box that is tiled in all three directions (test/testloopx_outer_n.par). TestLoopX_OuterN adds one marker per primitive to a vertex-centred (ord = 1) and a cell-centred (ord = 2) grid function, TestLoopX_OuterN_Check aborts the run if any point of the box, ghost layers included, was visited by neither or by both primitives, and the TSV cuts and norms pin the values (101 or 10 for testloop_gf_n1, 1 or 10 for testloop_gf_n2). The test was written for the fix of two coverage gaps: loop_outer_n_device used to span only the interior in the tangential directions of a band, so ghost edges beyond the band were never visited when ord < ghost_size, and loop_allmn_device used to shrink the tile instead of the component box, so the ord planes next to every interior tile face were skipped.
